"<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n- align: Record alignments with the user (plans, open questions, decisions) as structured documents\n- agent_resume: Resume a restored subagent idle in its own session\n- agent_models: Discover subagent backends, model IDs, and Claude effort options\n- agent_spawn: Spawn background subagents (non-blocking) and manage them by id\n- team_create: Create a team of role-based background workers who message each other\n- team_succeed: Replace a team's ended coordinator or monitor\n- vis_check: Check a draft vis html/svg/wireframe block: would it draw, its size against the budget, cramped text\n- project_verbs: run, reload, inspect and tear down your own worktree's running copy of the project (up, apply, logs, status…)\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>"
